WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
This is an important message from the U.S.

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.360
Department of Health and Human Services.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.660
Power outages and flooding can cause electrical hazards.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:10.460
Never touch a downed power line or anything in

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.140
contact with one. If a power line falls on

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.300
your car, remain inside unless the car catches fire

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.320
or authorities tell you to get out.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.780
Do not touch a person who has been electrocuted

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.240
without making sure the person is no longer in

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.780
contact with the electrical source.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:28.020
To learn more, call the CDC at 1-800

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.300
-CDC-INFO.
